l":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/astro-knots/commit/e4805021d0d0b3592720a8809e90d507f5d208c8","node_id":"C_kwDOPb7AGdoAKGU0ODA1MDIxZDBkMGIzNTkyNzIwYTg4MDllOTBkNTA3ZjVkMjA4Yzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lossless-group/astro-knots/commit/0e6dc0c38526318354bcc06265c26b24d13bff28","sha":"0e6dc0c38526318354bcc06265c26b24d13bff28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/astro-knots/commits/0e6dc0c38526318354bcc06265c26b24d13bff28"}],"sha":"e4805021d0d0b3592720a8809e90d507f5d208c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/astro-knots/commits/e4805021d0d0b3592720a8809e90d507f5d208c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mpstaton","id":5722,"login":"mpstaton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MjI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/astro-knots/commits/0e6dc0c38526318354bcc06265c26b24d13bff28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T18:39:48Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T18:39:48Z","email":"mpstaton@gmail.com","name":"mpstaton"},"message":"doc(lfm-spec, video-spec): extract Versatile-Component-Library-for-Video-Players, codify S→T→C\n\nThe LFM spec was carrying a long video-component section (§4.12 plus\nthe video-flavored portion of §4.23.6) that deserves its own home —\nthe family is mature enough to grow without forcing every change to\nride alongside unrelated LFM work. Extracted to a dedicated spec at\ncontext-v/specs/Versatile-Component-Library-for-Video-Players.md and\ntightened the parent LFM spec to point at it.\n\nThe new spec specifies the full video-component family — Tier A\nbare-URL auto-unfurl players (per provider), Tier B directive-form\nplayers, Tier C inline-substitution previews (LinkPreview__Video--*),\nTier D multi-URL containers (LinkRollup__* with Video children) —\nplus cross-cutting concerns (provider catalog, LinkPreviewData shape,\ntheme-token neutrality, lazy-load/facade strategy, aside compatibility,\nObsidian-portable fence-equivalence, opt-out, privacy posture).\n\nThe spec is built on the S→T→C model (Syntax → Trigger → Component)\ncodified as its foundational §3. Every new component or provider\nmust specify all three columns; PRs adding only Component code\nwithout specifying Syntax and Trigger are incomplete. The model is\nwalked end-to-end with a worked example tracing a YouTube playlist\nURL through bare-link classification to component dispatch.\n\nVersatile-Component-Library-for-Video-Players.md (new):\n- §3 The S→T→C Model with five subsections (the three stages, the\n  three syntax positions for video, the single-catalog principle, a\n  worked example, the acceptance criterion for new features)\n- §4 The Component Family in four tiers (A–D)\n- §5 Cross-Cutting Concerns (catalog, data shape, theme tokens,\n  facade strategy, aside matrix, fence-equivalence, opt-out, privacy)\n- §6 Implementation Phases 0–4\n- §7 Open Questions (5 design calls flagged for resolution during\n  implementation)\n- §8 References with backlinks to parent spec, catalog, theme blueprint,\n  test fixture, reference component implementations\n\nCodifying-...md (LFM parent spec) tightening:\n- §4.12 Zero-Friction Media Embeds collapsed from ~70 lines to ~30:\n  three-tier framing kept, provider catalog table preserved with\n  video rows pointing to the new spec, non-video providers (Spotify,\n  SoundCloud, Twitter, Figma, CodePen, Gist) stay full\n- §4.23.6 Type taxonomy table''s Video row gets a pointer to the new\n  spec for the full component family; the type-agnostic substitution\n  model (naming, format, aside, fence-equivalence, LinkPreviewData)\n  remains in §4.23.6 since it applies to all types\n- Phase 2 video components in workflow status reduced to a one-line\n  redirect to the new spec\n- Pointer format includes wikilink, full path, and grep/fzf fallback\n  in case the spec file moves\n\nsites/mpstaton-site:\n- Submodule pointer bumped to 143ea6b which ships the Shorts wrap-as-\n  aside change and the versatile :::youtube-short dispatcher (the\n  first use of the directive-form taxonomy this spec describes)\n\nFiles changed:\n- context-v/specs/Codifying-a-Comprehensive-Extended-Markdown-Flavor-and-Shared-Package.md\n- context-v/specs/Versatile-Component-Library-for-Video-Players.md\n- sites/mpstaton-site\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1c256f9f61a6819ee9e07a4c532c93dbaef99fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/astro-knots/git/trees/d1c256f9f61a6819ee9e07a4c532c93dbaef99fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lossless-group/astro-knots/git/commits/0e6dc0c38526318354bcc06265c26b24d13bff28","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5722?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpstaton/followers","foll