s/renovate%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wowothk/custom-authoring-mfe/commits/8b9a80eb04d8d0d5d383f5eb8a53477197c9f30e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-18T22:12:04Z","email":"29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"renovate[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-18T22:12:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): update dependency @tanstack/react-query to v4.40.0 (#2155)\n\n* fix(deps): update dependency @tanstack/react-query to v4.40.0\n\n* fix: npm was trying to install react-native which conflicted with React 18\n\nThe problem is that react-query 4.40.0 specifies an optional, unpinned peerDependency on react-native, and then it depends on @types/react 19, causing a conflict with our React 18. Putting an explicit dependency on the React types solves this. As would upgrading to React Query v5.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Braden MacDonald <braden@opencraft.com>","tree":{"sha":"65e9f305e88b2a55e5aea6165bfbb61ce1effb13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wowothk/custom-authoring-mfe/git/trees/65e9f305e88b2a55e5aea6165bfbb61ce1effb13"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wowothk/custom-authoring-mfe/git/commits/8b9a80eb04d8d0d5d383f5eb8a53477197c9f30e","verification":{"payload":"tree 65e9f305e88b2a55e5aea6165bfbb61ce1effb13\nparent a5c17452e75bb124a63362ba9dee443675e4331d\nauthor renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1750284724 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1750284724 +0000\n\nchore(deps): update dependency @tanstack/react-query to v4.40.0 (#2155)\n\n* fix(deps): update dependency @tanstack/react-query to v4.40.0\n\n* fix: npm was trying to install react-native which conflicted with React 18\n\nThe problem is that react-query 4.40.0 specifies an optional, unpinned peerDependency on react-native, and then it depends on @types/react 19, causing a conflict with our React 18. Putting an explicit dependency on the React types solves this. As would upgrading to React Query v5.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Braden MacDonald <braden@opencraft.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJoUzm0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlOcQAGV57TQPntP6oK3E1MtOgPNH\nBgfvVvkMZbSOwyiCQOjqLNeoCJZJ8tEOrxXjgR2tHkUoAky9g2rPnzgof0TqWV2O\n9vOREDpxi0CntRj1WN5XqYDGt1zN+5vwtWiOFY0UaokDj9CYfrrFl78Ojv2et8NQ\nCrpUHaPlJADFEedNS5hKNPE3y2j/04YZQVDvLuhlnFjKO8oQlagXVxe5KomzTyWZ\nus8JXMd7oRzO2bHYfWtbtO3J11IFETRtIMHUotvsoFqdbNv2RCtIZyK71XvvmkyN\nfG5UWdgjm66TG1rkyhCXGAHITOhAPG87FY545LsBo4yjVQccPEGP7hOw57lC35W8\nnVv/b2HZDtOYcP9SV0sEt/Qf6fduPdTq6AwX6yoLaAt1Yqjk+cZ/hgvhf/vsUngo\n9fSYPwOc5Fl3JPwLivq4j1sDQkfBuPlumfPEKq6Eq4ILwZAjIUlqTMWc7qsmI3yJ\n6PwEggCcPw7ONs/urtOGeS3D02Ej5TSXvSTIcagKNx7qID+U9LrVX+iF7AvYEJQS\nrg5HR3a6q07Yc6AqdwQmdrrkRpXT7OL9XURYP5nAoE/1nFBffDszAD5Wz++sTsn/\nqZO8clkICs8oTZOpjc4ngBkhszfOtLsWwjXDWbxniXeIjFypKXqRW3FP8xvXpJJY\nbeR+wEWUagbi36yQanZ4\n=FKdX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-08-13T10:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"w